{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to delete regular files in /var/tmp/inventory once older than seven days, using an enabled persistent systemd timer that runs daily. Verified cleanup behavior and persistence through a full node reboot.","actions_performed":["Created inventory-temp-cleanup.service with a seven-day age threshold.","Created and enabled inventory-temp-cleanup.timer with a daily schedule and persistent catch-up behavior.","Removed the expired inventory fixture while retaining the current fixture.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified its boot identity changed.","Confirmed the timer, unit files, inventory data, and cleanup behavior recovered after reboot."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Remove inventory temporary files after seven days while retaining newer files","command_ids":["cmd-31494fea0c244cbf","cmd-70f91a8d17cb4fe7","cmd-4aab0e03309e4895"],"summary":"The baseline contained expired.tmp and current.tmp. Cleanup removed the expired file and retained the current file; an independent post-reboot old/fresh probe produced the same result."},{"requirement":"Run inventory cleanup automatically each day","command_ids":["cmd-e77fa280e95e47c0","cmd-dc05ceb3807540a0","cmd-896c502a46ee4c8e"],"summary":"The timer is enabled and active, uses OnCalendar=daily with Persistent=true, has a scheduled next activation, and remained enabled and active after reboot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-dc05ceb3807540a0","cmd-6833bbcd193b475c","cmd-d8a70580a6604332","cmd-896c502a46ee4c8e","cmd-4aab0e03309e4895"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot ID was cce73776-a7f7-4f32-b822-95d105c52a64 with healthy automation and data. The safe reboot was acknowledged; afterward the boot ID was a108d304-0527-470e-85ab-191c1d50b1ea. The system returned to running state, the timer and data recovered, and cleanup succeeded post-restart."}]}
